*> Acceptance test, US13-5 core half (spec US13 scenario 5; FR-004; tasks T617; 07 §9): a saved world
*> folder copied to another path and opened there has every dimension, block, player record, mob and
*> ground item of the original. Alice changes a block in each dimension, a mob and a ground item are
*> placed in each, and Alice leaves from cobolcraft:subroutine (by the goto_pad at (6, 54, 12)).
 IDENTIFICATION DIVISION.
 PROGRAM-ID. ACC-US13-COPY-FOLDER.
 DATA DIVISION.
 WORKING-STORAGE SECTION.
 COPY TESTLIB.
 COPY CORESTATE.
 COPY COREAPI.
 COPY DIMENSIONS.
 COPY ETIDS.
 01 WS-COPY                PIC X(128) VALUE
     "rm -rf build/core-test-copied-world && cp -R build/core-test-world build/core-test-copied-world".
 01 WS-REMOVE              PIC X(64) VALUE "rm -rf build/core-test-world".
 01 WS-COPIED              PIC X(64) VALUE Z"build/core-test-copied-world".
 01 WS-CREATED             BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-ALICE-NAME          PIC X(16) VALUE "Alice".
 01 WS-LENGTH-5            BINARY-LONG VALUE 5.
 01 WS-ALICE               BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-ROW                 BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-DIM                 BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-X                   BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-Y                   BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-Z                   BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-STATE               BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-FACE                BINARY-LONG VALUE 1.
 01 WS-SEQUENCE            BINARY-LONG VALUE 1.
 01 WS-TYPE                BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-FX                  FLOAT-LONG.
 01 WS-FY                  FLOAT-LONG.
 01 WS-FZ                  FLOAT-LONG.
 01 WS-VX                  FLOAT-LONG VALUE 0.
 01 WS-VY                  FLOAT-LONG VALUE 0.
 01 WS-VZ                  FLOAT-LONG VALUE 0.
 01 WS-YAW                 FLOAT-SHORT VALUE 0.
 01 WS-ITEM                BINARY-LONG VALUE 7.
 01 WS-COUNT               BINARY-LONG VALUE 2.
 01 WS-DELAY               BINARY-LONG VALUE 0.
 01 WS-TEXT                PIC X(8192).
 01 WS-WORLD-BEFORE        PIC X(8192).
 01 WS-ALICE-BEFORE        PIC X(8192).
 01 WS-BLOCKS-BEFORE       PIC X(256).
 01 WS-BLOCKS              PIC X(256).
 01 WS-EDIT                PIC -(9)9.
 PROCEDURE DIVISION.
     CALL "TEST-SETTINGS" USING CORE-SETTINGS
     MOVE 0 TO CS-HOSTILE-MOBS CS-WEATHER-CHANGES
     MOVE 2 TO CS-VIEW-DISTANCE
     MOVE 1 TO CS-EXTRA-DIMENSIONS
     CALL "TEST-OPEN-WORLD" USING CORE-SETTINGS
     MOVE 16001 TO CW-TIME
     CALL "TEST-JOIN" USING WS-ALICE-NAME WS-LENGTH-5 WS-ALICE
     MOVE DIM-MAIN TO WS-DIM
     MOVE 6 TO WS-X MOVE 54 TO WS-Y MOVE 12 TO WS-Z
     MOVE TRAVEL-PAD-STATE TO WS-STATE
     CALL "WORLD-SET-BLOCK" USING WS-DIM WS-X WS-Y WS-Z WS-STATE
     MOVE 3 TO WS-X MOVE 58 TO WS-Y MOVE 3 TO WS-Z
     MOVE 15 TO WS-STATE
     CALL "WORLD-SET-BLOCK" USING WS-DIM WS-X WS-Y WS-Z WS-STATE
     MOVE ET-SODGRAZER TO WS-TYPE
     MOVE 40.5 TO WS-FX MOVE 55 TO WS-FY MOVE -10.5 TO WS-FZ
     CALL "MOB-SPAWN" USING WS-DIM WS-TYPE WS-FX WS-FY WS-FZ WS-YAW WS-ROW
     CALL "GI-SPAWN" USING WS-DIM WS-FX WS-FY WS-FZ WS-VX WS-VY WS-VZ WS-ITEM WS-COUNT WS-DELAY
         WS-ROW
     MOVE DIM-SUBROUTINE TO WS-DIM
     MOVE -7 TO WS-X MOVE 45 TO WS-Y MOVE 9 TO WS-Z
     MOVE 17 TO WS-STATE
     CALL "WORLD-SET-BLOCK" USING WS-DIM WS-X WS-Y WS-Z WS-STATE
     MOVE ET-ABEND TO WS-TYPE
     MOVE -40.5 TO WS-FX MOVE 36 TO WS-FY MOVE 10.5 TO WS-FZ
     CALL "MOB-SPAWN" USING WS-DIM WS-TYPE WS-FX WS-FY WS-FZ WS-YAW WS-ROW
     CALL "GI-SPAWN" USING WS-DIM WS-FX WS-FY WS-FZ WS-VX WS-VY WS-VZ WS-ITEM WS-COUNT WS-DELAY
         WS-ROW
     MOVE 6 TO WS-X MOVE 54 TO WS-Y MOVE 12 TO WS-Z
     CALL "TEST-USE-ON" USING WS-ALICE WS-X WS-Y WS-Z WS-FACE WS-SEQUENCE
     CALL "TEST-ACCEPT-TELEPORT" USING WS-ALICE
     CALL "TEST-PLAYER-SNAPSHOT" USING CN-PLAYER(WS-ALICE) WS-ALICE-BEFORE
     CALL "CORE-CONN-CLOSED" USING WS-ALICE
     PERFORM DESCRIBE-BLOCKS
     MOVE WS-BLOCKS TO WS-BLOCKS-BEFORE
     CALL "TEST-WORLD-SNAPSHOT" USING WS-WORLD-BEFORE
     CALL "CORE-SAVE"
     CALL "SYSTEM" USING WS-COPY
     CALL "SYSTEM" USING WS-REMOVE
     CALL "CORE-WORLD-OPEN" USING WS-COPIED CORE-SETTINGS WS-CREATED

     MOVE "acceptance US13-5 given a world folder copied to another path when opened there then "
         & "both dimensions and every block are the same" TO TL-CASE
     PERFORM DESCRIBE-BLOCKS
     MOVE SPACES TO WS-TEXT
     MOVE WS-CREATED TO WS-EDIT
     STRING "created " FUNCTION TRIM(WS-EDIT) " dimensions" DELIMITED BY SIZE INTO WS-TEXT
     MOVE CW-DIM-COUNT TO WS-EDIT
     STRING FUNCTION TRIM(WS-TEXT) " " FUNCTION TRIM(WS-EDIT) " blocks " FUNCTION TRIM(WS-BLOCKS)
         DELIMITED BY SIZE INTO WS-TEXT
     MOVE SPACES TO TL-EXPECTED
     STRING "created 0 dimensions 2 blocks " FUNCTION TRIM(WS-BLOCKS-BEFORE) DELIMITED BY SIZE
         INTO TL-EXPECTED
     PERFORM CHECK

     MOVE "acceptance US13-5 the copied world has the same mobs and ground items" TO TL-CASE
     CALL "TEST-WORLD-SNAPSHOT" USING WS-TEXT
     MOVE WS-WORLD-BEFORE TO TL-EXPECTED
     PERFORM CHECK

     MOVE "acceptance US13-5 the copied world has the same player record: Alice rejoins in "
         & "cobolcraft:subroutine as she left" TO TL-CASE
     CALL "TEST-JOIN" USING WS-ALICE-NAME WS-LENGTH-5 WS-ALICE
     CALL "TEST-PLAYER-SNAPSHOT" USING CN-PLAYER(WS-ALICE) WS-TEXT
     MOVE WS-ALICE-BEFORE TO TL-EXPECTED
     PERFORM CHECK
     STOP RUN.

 DESCRIBE-BLOCKS.
     MOVE SPACES TO WS-BLOCKS
     MOVE DIM-MAIN TO WS-DIM
     MOVE 3 TO WS-X MOVE 58 TO WS-Y MOVE 3 TO WS-Z
     PERFORM ADD-BLOCK
     MOVE 6 TO WS-X MOVE 54 TO WS-Y MOVE 12 TO WS-Z
     PERFORM ADD-BLOCK
     MOVE DIM-SUBROUTINE TO WS-DIM
     MOVE -7 TO WS-X MOVE 45 TO WS-Y MOVE 9 TO WS-Z
     PERFORM ADD-BLOCK.

 ADD-BLOCK.
     CALL "WORLD-GET-BLOCK" USING WS-DIM WS-X WS-Y WS-Z WS-STATE
     MOVE WS-STATE TO WS-EDIT
     STRING FUNCTION TRIM(WS-BLOCKS) " " FUNCTION TRIM(WS-EDIT) DELIMITED BY SIZE INTO WS-BLOCKS.

 CHECK.
     MOVE "T" TO TL-MODE
     MOVE WS-TEXT TO TL-OBSERVED
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT.
 END PROGRAM ACC-US13-COPY-FOLDER.

 COPY CORETEST.
